# SRG-APP-000225-WSR-000074  -  CAT II
# The web server must augment re-creation to a stable and known baseline.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000225-WSR-000074
group:           V-206404
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       manual
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-001190
control_rev5:    SC-24

contribution:    Splunk Enterprise holds its configuration in plain .conf files that can be
                 captured and restored wholesale, and where a deployment server is used it
                 serves apps to clients from a server-held repository. Nothing in the
                 product hinders reinstallation to a known baseline, which is what this
                 requirement's finding condition turns on, and there is no setting that
                 would either permit or prohibit it.

external:        Backup and restore of the configuration and index data - organizational
                 backup procedure
external:        Version control or configuration management of the .conf baseline -
                 configuration management system
external:        Where a deployment server is used, the contents and integrity of the app
                 repository it serves - deployment server administration
external:        Reinstallation media and the installation procedure itself -
                 organizational procedure

manual_reason:   The check's finding condition is that the product prohibits reinstallation
                 to a known state, and Splunk Enterprise does not. The attached keys are
                 not operator-set hardening values: app.conf's install_source_checksum and
                 install_source_local_checksum are populated automatically by the installer
                 and the spec directs that they not be set by hand, and the
                 serverclass.conf repository settings apply only where a deployment server
                 is in use, so requiring them would fail a correctly built single instance.
                 No condition over configuration decides this requirement.

citation:        app.conf.spec:158-167 (install_source_checksum and
                 install_source_local_checksum: "Splunk Enterprise automatically populates
                 this value upon install. Do not set this value explicitly within your
                 app!"); app.conf.spec:124-127 (state = disabled|enabled, default enabled);
                 serverclass.conf.spec:68-71 (repositoryLocation), :107-113
                 (targetRepositoryLocation), :356-362 (stateOnClient =
                 enabled|disabled|noop); splunk-launch.conf.spec:67-73 (SPLUNK_DB)
finding:         Not decidable from Splunk configuration: the product neither prohibits nor
                 hinders reinstallation to a known baseline and exposes no setting bearing
                 on it, so the application's share of this requirement is satisfied by
                 product design and the baseline re-creation procedure is assessed against
                 the organization's backup, restore and configuration management practice.
